import java.util.Scanner;
public class HW2 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

    Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
    System.out.println("Enter a word:");
    String var = sc.nextLine();

    for (int i = 0; i < var.length(); i++){
        System.out.println(var.charAt(i));
    
    }
    sc.close();
    }
// I figured out how to do this by going to google for some guidance. To translate, my code is taking input from the user that is in the form of a string. We start at i=0 (the first letter of the word), and we stop once we hit the number of characters the entered word has. And we are going forward throguh the word, so I used i++. I used the charAt(i) to get the character at each position i. This allows the terminal to print each letter of the word on a new line.  
